<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">June Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1924</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The June Revolution was an uprising in Albania in June 1924 that drove <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">Ahmet Zogu</a> from power and brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> and reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fan-noli">Fan Noli</a> to the head of the government. Noli promised land reform and democratic change but failed to win foreign recognition or hold elections. In December 1924 Zogu returned with Yugoslav support and White Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> and overthrew him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/june-revolution-albania.jpg" alt="June Revolution" width="320" height="170" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_June_1924_revolution.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
